Only the fill simulator and the four dataclasses it needs were taken. The
upstream Engine, SQLite layer, CLI, MCP server, backtester and benchmark
tooling were deliberately left behind -- this project keeps its own
Portfolio, price feed and dashboard.

Taken from upstream:
    models.py     <- pm_trader/models.py    (OrderBookLevel, OrderBook, Fill, FillResult)
    orderbook.py  <- pm_trader/orderbook.py (calculate_fee, simulate_buy_fill, simulate_sell_fill)

Written for this project (not upstream):
    books.py      CLOB order-book + fee-rate fetching
    __init__.py   public surface

DEVIATIONS FROM UPSTREAM
------------------------
1. Imports rewritten from `pm_trader.models` to the local `.models`.

2. Fee basis corrected in simulate_buy_fill.  Upstream passes `total_cost`
   (USD) as the `size` argument on the buy path but `total_shares` on the
   sell path.  Upstream's own README documents the formula as
   `bps/10000 x min(price, 1-price) x shares`, so the buy path understated
   the fee by a factor of avg_price -- at 30 cents a buy was charged ~70%
   less than the equivalent sell.  The buy path now passes `total_shares`,
   matching both the sell path and the documented formula.  Marked inline
   with a DEVIATION comment.

